## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates practical observability expertise across a CNPA stack, requiring candidates to instrument distributed systems, maintain context propagation, and correlate performance issues with specific infrastructure bottlenecks. Tests ability to translate monitoring concepts into actionable debugging strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Distributed tracing across HTTP, PostgreSQL, Kafka, and Redis
- Context propagation using correlation IDs in headers
- Tail-based vs. head-based sampling strategies
- End-to-end latency analysis (p95/p99, tail latency)
- Backpressure detection (Kafka consumer lag, Redis cache misses)
- Canary deployment with automated rollback criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// OpenTelemetry instrumentation setup
const { NodeSDK } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-node');
const { getNodeAutoInstrumentations } = require('@opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node');

const sdk = new NodeSDK({
  instrumentations: [getNodeAutoInstrumentations()],
  sampler: new TraceIdRatioBasedSampler(0.15), // 15% sampling
  resource: new Resource({
    'service.name': 'api-service',
    'service.version': process.env.APP_VERSION
  })
});

sdk.start();
```

